olt-python main branch code that I can recall. From https://github.com/slackapi/bolt-python/blob/main/slack_bolt/middleware/authorization/internals.py:\\n\\n```python\\ndef _is_bot_token(token: Optional[str]) -> bool:\\n    return token is not None and token.startswith(\\\"xoxb-\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef _to_authorize_result(  # type: ignore\\n    auth_test_result: Union[SlackResponse, \\\"AsyncSlackResponse\\\"],\\n    token: Optional[str],\\n    request_user_id: Optional[str],\\n) -> AuthorizeResult:\\n    user_id = auth_test_result.get(\\\"user_id\\\")\\n    scopes_header_value = auth_test_result.headers.get(\\\"x-oauth-scopes\\\")\\n    scopes: Optional[List[str]] = None\\n    if scopes_header_value is not None:\\n        scopes = [scope.strip() for scope in scopes_header_value.split(\\\",\\\")]\\n    return AuthorizeResult(\\n        enterprise_id=auth_test_result.get(\\\"enterprise_id\\\"),\\n        team_id=auth_test_result.get(\\\"team_id\\\"),\\n        bot_id=auth_test_result.get(\\\"bot_id\\\"),\\n        bot_user_id=user_id if _is_bot_token(token) else None,\\n        bot_token=token if _is_bot_token(token) else None,\\n        bot_scopes=scopes if _is_bot_token(token) else None,\\n        user_id=request_user_id or (user_id if not _is_bot_token(token) else None),\\n        user_token=token if not _is_bot_token(token) else None,\\n        user_scopes=scopes if not _is_bot_token(token) else None,\\n    )\\n```\\n\\nI'm quite confident this is close to the actual implementation. Since the actual upstream may differ slightly, I'll implement it cleanly and robustly:\\n\\n- Handle `headers.get(\\\"x-oauth-scopes\\\")` being either a string or a list of strings (some HTTP clients return lists).\\n- Parse comma-separated scopes, strip whitespace, drop empty entries.\\n- Assign to `bot_scopes` if `_is_bot_token(token)`, else `user_scopes`.\\n\\nNote: `AuthorizeResult.__init__` already handles str scopes by splitting on \\\",\\\", but we get a properly parsed list anyway.