ributes correctly.\\\"\\n\\nThe async version `AsyncSingleTeamAuthorization` uses the same `_to_authorize_result` from `.internals` (sync internals — the note says the file intentionally avoids Async references but uses typeignore Union). So changing `_to_authorize_result` handles both.\\n\\nLet me verify how the aiohttp-based AsyncSlackResponse headers look. In slack_sdk's async base_client:\\n\\n```python\\nreturn AsyncSlackResponse(\\n    client=self,\\n    http_verb=http_verb,\\n    api_url=api_url,\\n    req_args=req_args,\\n    data=data,\\n    headers=dict(response.headers),\\n    status_code=response.status,\\n)\\n```\\n\\n`dict(response.headers)` for aiohttp's CIMultiDict gives Dict[str, str]. For httpx, `dict(headers)` gives Dict[str, str]. So mostly str values. But urllib: let me check.\\n\\nLet me now check slack_sdk 3.30.0's base_client to see how headers are passed.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"Now let me check how slack_sdk builds the response headers (to know their types):"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_83d4b6bbca23474c8934185a","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"python - <<'EOF'\nimport inspect\nfrom slack_sdk.web import base_client\nsrc = inspect.getsource(base_client)\nimport re\n# find where SlackResponse is constructed\nidx = 0\nfor m in re.finditer(r\"SlackResponse\\(\", src):\n    start = max(0, m.start()-800)\n    print(src[m.start()-200:m.start()+400])\n    print(\"======\")\nEOF"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"harbor-endpoint","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":1070,"output":3372,"cacheRead":17152,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":3259,"totalTokens":21594,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788490636069,"responseId":"gen-1788490636-KuvEdglMM77EphRxyNfj","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
