uses the same `_to_authorize_result` helper, the async app gets the same behavior with no additional changes.\n\n3. **`tests/mock_web_api_server.py`** — the mock `auth.test` endpoint now returns the `x-oauth-scopes` header (`chat:write,commands` for bot tokens, `chat:write,search:read` for user tokens).\n\n4. Tests added for both sync and async paths verifying `authorize_result.bot_scopes` / `user_scopes`.\n\nAll tests pass: slack_bolt (115), slack_bolt_async (76), scenario_tests (222), scenario_tests_async (221).","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"The implementation is complete and matches the upstream fix (which landed in bolt-python v1.21.2). Let me summarize the changes.\\n\\nSummary of what was done:\\n\\n1. **`slack_bolt/middleware/authorization/internals.py`** — `_to_authorize_result()` now reads the `x-oauth-scopes` HTTP response header from the `auth.test` API response and:\\n   - assigns it to `bot_scopes` when the token is a bot token (`xoxb-`)\\n   - assigns it to `user_scopes` when the token is a user token (`xoxp-`)\\n   - The `AuthorizeResult` constructor converts the comma-separated string into a `List[str]`.\\n\\n2. Since `AsyncSingleTeamAuthorization` reuses the same `_to_authorize_result` helper, the async app gets the same behavior with no additional changes.\\n\\n3. **`tests/mock_web_api_server.py`** — the mock `auth.test` endpoint now returns the `x-oauth-scopes` header (`chat:write,commands` for bot tokens, `chat:write,search:read` for user tokens).\\n\\n4. Tests added for both sync and async paths verifying `authorize_result.bot_scopes` / `user_scopes`.\\n\\nAll tests pass: slack_bolt (115), slack_bolt_async (76), scenario_tests (222), scenario_tests_async (221).\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"The implementation is complete. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n## Changes\n\n### 1. Core fix — `slack_bolt/middleware/authorization/internals.py`\nThe `_to_authorize_result()` helper (used by `SingleTeamAuthorization`) now extracts the OAuth scopes from the `x-oauth-scopes` response header of the `auth.test` API call and assigns them based on token type:\n- **Bot token (`xoxb-`)** → scopes stored in `bot_scopes`\n- **User token (`xoxp-`)** → scopes stored in `user_scopes`\n\n`AuthorizeResult` converts the comma-separated header string (e.g. `\"chat:write,commands\"`) into a proper `List[str]`. Since `AsyncSingleTeamAuthorization` shares this same helper, **both `slack_bolt.App` and `slack_bolt.async_app.AsyncApp` get the behavior automatically** — the scopes appear in `req.context.authorize_result.bot_scopes` / `.user_scopes`, matching what `MultiTeamsAuthorization` already provides via installation stores.\n\n### 2. Test infrastructure — `tests/mock_web_api_server.py`\nThe mock `auth.test` endpoint now returns the `x-oauth-scopes` header (`chat:write,commands` for bot tokens, `chat:write,search:read` for user tokens), mirroring real Slack API behavior.\n\n### 3. Tests added\n- `tests/slack_bolt/middleware/authorization/test_single_team_authorization.py::test_success_pattern_with_bot_scopes` — verifies `bot_scopes == [\"chat:write\", \"commands\"]` and `user_scopes is None`\n- `tests/slack_bolt_async/middleware/authorization/test_single_team_authorization.py::test_success_pattern_with_bot_scopes` — same verification through the async path (real `auth.test` call against the mock server)\n\n## Verification\n\n```\nbot token  -> bot_scopes: ['chat:write', 'commands'] | user_scopes: None\nuser token -> bot_scopes: None | user_scopes: ['chat:write', 'search:read']\n```\n\nAll test suites pass with no regressions:\n- `tests/slack_bolt/` — 115 passed\n- `tests/slack_bolt_async/` — 76 passed\n- `tests/scenario_tests/` — 222 passed\n- `tests/scenario_tests_async/` — 221 passed\n\nExisting authorization behavior is untouched — the only change is the addition of the two scope properties to the authorize result, so you can now programmatically check e.g. `authorize_result.bot_scopes` before executing features that require specific OAuth grants."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"harbor-endpoint","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":1367,"output":846,"cacheRead":38528,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":287,"totalTokens":40741,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1788491278207,"responseId":"gen-1788491278-i8W2ddWSq84pejBwHxmA","rawStopReason":"stop"}],"willRetry":false}
